Z||000000||JayUSA77||10-22-2001||12:49 AM||||this is what i need guys, oh let me first say how is everyone doing? i havent had much time to go on but when i do im glad to hear your guys opionions. N-E ways back the subject.  OkaY my 86 GT has a 4 speed. What i need to know is how fast IN MPH will each gear go to at 6K RPM.  I know you guys would say go drive and find out but my car is currently on jackstands and will stay that way all the way up until my V-8 is in it.  So i need to know what MPH at 6k rpm in first gear,second,third and forth is.   Also what is the top speed of the forth gear at 6K RPM.  Thanks for the info and i hope i didnt confuse you guys that much<BR>j<BR><P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000001||Hank is Here||10-22-2001||01:00 AM||||Need more info.  What is the RPO code for the gear ratio and what tire size does it have--tire size affects speeed for at a given RPM<P>Hank||||reg||1
Z||000002||JayUSA77||10-22-2001||01:10 AM||||in the back it will have 17 inch wheels with low profile tires and around 245 width.<BR>J<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Pontiaddict||10-22-2001||01:53 AM||||Here are the apporximate speeds for an 86 with 245/45/17's on it. No guarantees on how close I actually am.<P>1st@6k = 38mph<BR>2nd@6k = 63mph<BR>3rd@6k = 103mph<BR>4th@6k = 160mph<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Philphine||10-22-2001||07:56 AM||||could someone do the same with a 4:10 with about a 25 1/2" diameter tire or give the formula to figure it out?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Orville||10-22-2001||10:37 AM||||There are a couple of tire/wheel sites that<BR>give formulas but I lost their links, so I'll<BR>just give you them. MPH= (RPM x circumference x 60) divided by (top gear ratio x diff ratio<BR>x 63371.4). RPM= (MPH x top gear ratio x diff<BR>ratio x 63371.4) divided by (circumference x<BR>60). Circumference is given in inches. Maybe<BR>it's easier just driving the car and checking <BR>the gauges.<BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tina||10-22-2001||10:07 PM||||Just a thought, in case this is going to be your daily driver.<BR>Don't really recall rmp's anymore,but I don't know how often I caught myself attempting to shift into 4th on the highway.(60-70mph)<BR>Problem was, I was already there.<BR>(tranny was a muncy 4.10)<P>Tina<BR>||||reg||1
